{"claim_id": "S21-01", "task_id": "item1-refetch", "claim": "All five external sources the v1.3 notice cites were re-fetched on 2026-09-18, all HTTP 200. The vdPS AIF PDF, the arXiv 0902.1702v5 PDF, the Jimbo EMS PDF and the companion v1.2 PDF served by Zenodo are each BYTE-IDENTICAL to the local copy (sha256 equality). No source was NOT RE-FETCHED. Downloads went to a temp directory outside the repository: a re-fetch is verification, not acquisition.", "label": "VERIFIED", "evidence_type": "computation", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "scripts/item1_refetch.py", "output_hash": "c6860cc28d73c6a83ca05a9037393ea0c63f19ea25c21ff9c48055f91348782f"}
{"claim_id": "S21-02", "task_id": "item1-zenodo-dois", "claim": "Companion v1.2 = Zenodo record 20481592, version DOI 10.5281/zenodo.20481592, CONCEPT DOI 10.5281/zenodo.20455089 - the two differ, so a citation of the exact text the notice corrects must use the version DOI. metadata.version = \"1.2\"; the file checksum Zenodo reports matches the local md5.", "label": "VERIFIED", "evidence_type": "computation", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "scripts/item1b_resolve.py", "output_hash": "83e868f75b1f7ca10b7c148d95db73b2bd51384ac28df5efc5c3bd421abdf5ce"}
{"claim_id": "S21-03", "task_id": "item1-dlmf-version", "claim": "DLMF section 32.2, cited by v1.2 for the PV normalisation and at 32.2(vi) Eq. 32.2.33 for the PV->PIII degeneration, was fetched at Version 1.2.8, release date 2026-09-15. The DLMF is a living document; version and release date must travel with the citation.", "label": "VERIFIED", "evidence_type": "computation", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "scripts/item1b_resolve.py", "output_hash": "83e868f75b1f7ca10b7c148d95db73b2bd51384ac28df5efc5c3bd421abdf5ce"}
{"claim_id": "S21-04", "task_id": "item3-arxiv-licence", "claim": "The arXiv abstract page for 0902.1702 prints the licence http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/ - arXiv's DEFAULT licence, which grants arXiv distribution rights and grants third parties NO redistribution right. The arXiv PDF therefore may not be committed or deposited. The three Zenodo companion records print cc-by-4.0. The AIF item page carries no CC string (the PDF title page prints \"tous droits reserves\") and the EMS article page could not be read: both stay NOT CHECKED. No licence determination was made and no exclusion was changed.", "label": "INSPECTED", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "scripts/item3_licences.py", "output_hash": "0eee556b5374e6cff2d730050aef2de512714e7c539d8a0e22f362b926e4cb31"}
{"claim_id": "S21-05", "task_id": "item2-quotes", "claim": "Thirteen quote rows checked against page images, one image per message: vdPS pp. 2634, 2635, 2637, 2655; Jimbo p. 1152 including hypothesis (A1)_PV \"theta_0, theta_t not in Z\"; companion v1.2 printed pp. 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 10. All MATCH except the location of family (4.1). Hypotheses were treated as in scope, not only theorem statements.", "label": "VERIFIED", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "manual page-image reads, tabulated in outputs/item2_quotes.md", "output_hash": "dac690177ead95cd5863deabcf09c467779694fddedb6d0736f1a28bf2c32367"}
{"claim_id": "S21-06", "task_id": "item2-family41-page", "claim": "DIFFERS: the notice and the vdPS letter both locate the family as \"family (4.1) on p. 2655\". The LABEL (4.1) is displayed on p. 2654; only the entries, including the b(z) being corrected, are printed on p. 2655. The mathematics is unaffected. Recommended wording: \"the entry b(z) of family (4.1) (displayed p. 2654), printed on p. 2655\". Matters more in the letter, which goes to the authors.", "label": "VERIFIED", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "outputs/item2_quotes.md", "output_hash": "dac690177ead95cd5863deabcf09c467779694fddedb6d0736f1a28bf2c32367"}
{"claim_id": "S21-07", "task_id": "item2-c5-incomplete", "claim": "C5 states its list of affected passages was \"located by a full-text pass over v1.2 and read from page images\" and lists five. Reading the page images found FOUR FURTHER passages that depend on the apparency claim and appear nowhere in the notice: Theorem 3.1, Remark 3.2 (\"the monodromy at the finite singularities is exactly trivial by algebra\"), Remark 4.2 (\"theta_1 = theta_2 = 0 (apparent singularities), the standard connection formula degenerates ... consistent with the failure of all tested PSLQ identification bases\"), and Remark 6.7. Remark 4.2 is load-bearing: it is the companion's explanation of the PSLQ nulls. C5's completeness assertion is therefore not supported as it stands.", "label": "STRUCTURAL", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "outputs/item2_quotes.md", "output_hash": "dac690177ead95cd5863deabcf09c467779694fddedb6d0736f1a28bf2c32367"}
{"claim_id": "S21-08", "task_id": "item2-theorem31", "claim": "v1.2 Theorem 3.1 (printed pp. 4-5, read from a rendered page image) ALREADY PROVES C1's local analysis: its Step 1 computes p_0 = a'(s_k)/a'(s_k) = 1 and q_0 = 0, giving I(rho) = rho(rho-1) + p_0 rho + q_0 = rho^2 = 0; Step 3 puts the logarithm in y_2 only; and Step 4 DISPLAYS THE MONODROMY as [[1, 2*pi*i],[0,1]], which is unipotent and not the identity. Theorem 3.1(ii) claims only that the EFFECTIVE monodromy on the connection coefficient M_11 is trivial, because the unipotent action fixes y_1 - a different and weaker statement than apparency. Consequences: (a) C1 corrects Remark 2.2's GENERAL claim about the roots of chi, not a gap in section 3; (b) the notice as drafted would lead a reader to take section 3 as collateral damage of C1, which this evidence does not support. Theorem 3.1(ii)'s CORRECTNESS was not re-derived and is not asserted here.", "label": "STRUCTURAL", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "outputs/item2_quotes.md", "output_hash": "dac690177ead95cd5863deabcf09c467779694fddedb6d0736f1a28bf2c32367"}
{"claim_id": "S21-09", "task_id": "item4-consistency", "claim": "Internal consistency: every claim_id the notice cites exists and is not superseded (PASS); no sentence asserts anything as author-confirmed that is not, and the hedges \"had not been sent\" and \"No published erratum is known to us\" are intact (PASS). Two failures: S4-06 and S5B-C6 carry review = None in the corpus while the notice's support table shows them cold - VERIFY-S14.md and _deps_table.md show the cold read did happen by route \"D - corroborated\", so the CORPUS rows are stale and the notice is right; and C4 reads \"Four points must accompany this table\" then enumerates seven. A vacuity pre-check on injected bad data confirmed the scan fires.", "label": "VERIFIED", "evidence_type": "computation", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "scripts/item4_consistency.py", "output_hash": "23a525034a16f717a5d28c39a51ad7f161f036874d941f9ad61df205decf5f4c"}
{"claim_id": "S21-10", "task_id": "item4-r1-107-false", "claim": "CORRECTION TO MY OWN CLAIM R1-107, which stated that after last round's .gitignore zero third-party bytes would be staged. Re-derived in a separate invocation: \"git add -n -A -- sessions/2026-09-17\" stages 411 paths, 17 of them image/pdf/html, of which NINE are third party (vdps_p2634.png, vdps_p2635.png, jimbo_p1152.png, four CT-S10-COLDREAD2/dlmf_5_11*.html, two CT-S9-PVPARAMS jimbo page images). The other eight are the operator's own CC-BY-4.0 companion pages and this project's theorem.pdf. The CT-S18 and CT-S19 packet images ARE already excluded, sitting under packet/pages/; an earlier draft of DEPOSIT-READY.md listed them as exposed and re-deriving the count corrected it. This is a COMMIT blocker, not a deposit blocker. The packet said \"change no exclusion\", so .gitignore was not edited. R1-107 needs amendment or supersession.", "label": "VERIFIED", "evidence_type": "computation", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "git add -n -A, re-derived separately; DEPOSIT-READY.md", "output_hash": "3adab8dd35b4c25469a09d8856fec61d922a0c74a0ac09688c436b8c100b2500"}
{"claim_id": "S21-11", "task_id": "item2-self-caught-notchecked", "claim": "SELF-CAUGHT DEFECT: the first draft of item2_quotes.md recorded Remark 6.1 (C5 row 4) as NOT CHECKED on the stated ground that its page image was unavailable. I had not opened the image. The page-number mapping I reasoned from (printed = N + 1) was correct and the conclusion was still wrong: companion_v12_p7.png is printed p. 8 and Remark 6.1 is on it, quoted verbatim as \"derived from the WKB and apparent-singularity data\", which MATCHES. A NOT CHECKED status is only honest when something was attempted and failed; otherwise it should say not attempted. Recommend an eighth P0 line.", "label": "INSPECTED", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "outputs/item2_quotes.md", "output_hash": "dac690177ead95cd5863deabcf09c467779694fddedb6d0736f1a28bf2c32367"}
{"claim_id": "S21-12", "task_id": "verdict", "claim": "VERDICT: the v1.3 notice is NOT READY for deposit on this evidence. Six items must resolve first (M1 C5 incompleteness and the Theorem 3.1 understatement; M2 the letter-status placeholder in C3, currently true but false the moment the letter is sent; M3 the stale review fields; M4 \"four\" vs seven; M5 the p. 2654/2655 location; M6 the commit-side exclusion hole). None touches the mathematics of C1-C5. Only M1 requires a judgement rather than an edit.", "label": "INSPECTED", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "DEPOSIT-READY.md", "output_hash": "3adab8dd35b4c25469a09d8856fec61d922a0c74a0ac09688c436b8c100b2500"}
{"claim_id": "S21-13", "task_id": "m1-theta-survives", "claim": "The formal monodromy exponents theta_1 = theta_2 = 0 SURVIVE C1. They record the difference of the local exponents at each finite singularity, and both exponents are 0 by the double root of the indicial equation rho^2 = 0 - which is precisely what C1 establishes and what v1.2 Theorem 3.1(i) had already computed and certified numerically at dps=150. Apparency is not required for theta = 0; theta = 0 is exactly the resonant case in which logarithms occur. Consequently every passage of v1.2 whose operative premise is theta_1 = theta_2 = 0 is untouched by this notice, including C2, which relies on those values.", "label": "STRUCTURAL", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "page images of v1.2 printed pp. 5, 6; C:\\LocalWork\\siarc-relay-bridge\\sessions\\2026-09-17\\CT-R1-AUDIT\\DRAFT-COMPANION-v1.3-NOTICE.md", "output_hash": "f3ac6d41a1ed779bad0c600a93dcf23f683863cdaf41395f8262f1839c3bebde"}
{"claim_id": "S21-14", "task_id": "m1-remark42-excluded", "claim": "Remark 4.2 does NOT belong in C5. Its operative premise is theta_1 = theta_2 = 0, not apparency: what degenerates is the Jimbo connection formula, through gamma functions at the formal monodromy exponents. The phrase \"(apparent singularities)\" is a parenthetical gloss. Decisive internal evidence: v1.2 states the SAME fact without any gloss at section 7.1 item 3, \"The standard Jimbo connection formula degenerates at theta_1 = theta_2 = 0, leaving no known closed-form expression.\" Since theta = 0 survives C1 (S21-13), the PSLQ-null explanation is unaffected.", "label": "STRUCTURAL", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "page images of v1.2 printed pp. 7, 10", "output_hash": "f3ac6d41a1ed779bad0c600a93dcf23f683863cdaf41395f8262f1839c3bebde"}
{"claim_id": "S21-15", "task_id": "m1-remark67-excluded", "claim": "Remark 6.7 does NOT belong in C5, and not for the same reason as Remark 4.2. It rests on Theorem 3.1(ii), not on apparency and not on the theta values: the printed parenthetical glosses \"apparent\" as \"trivial local monodromy ON M_11 = V_quad; Theorem 3.1\", and the consequence drawn is likewise about M_11 (\"by any monodromy-based argument\"). Theorem 3.1(ii) is unadjudicated in this work, so no verdict is recorded and the passage is listed among the deliberate exclusions with its reason.", "label": "STRUCTURAL", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "page image of v1.2 printed p. 10", "output_hash": "f3ac6d41a1ed779bad0c600a93dcf23f683863cdaf41395f8262f1839c3bebde"}
{"claim_id": "S21-16", "task_id": "m1-remark32-included", "claim": "Remark 3.2 DOES belong in C5. Verbatim from the page image: \"the monodromy at the finite singularities is exactly trivial by algebra\" - stated flatly, WITHOUT the M_11 qualifier that Theorem 3.1(ii) carries, so it asserts apparency. Per the operator ruling the C5 line records the dependency only; this notice takes no position on whether the sentence is correct, not having checked it.", "label": "INSPECTED", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "page image of v1.2 printed p. 6", "output_hash": "f3ac6d41a1ed779bad0c600a93dcf23f683863cdaf41395f8262f1839c3bebde"}
